  RETENTION -- the fraction of the GAIN that survived, which is what
  credit-oracle scored (0.84 broadcast -> 1.03 targeted). Unlike the raw
  gap this is not confounded by the mask's learning-rate cost.
    broadcast  not in this focus set
    oracle     AB -1.347 +/- 1.132    keep 0.089 +/- 0.901
    derived    not in this focus set
    latch      not in this focus set

  SEPARATION -- does the index DISTINGUISH the two lessons, regardless of
  which slot got which name? Raw agreement cannot answer this: the slots are
  UNLABELLED, so a fixed slot->half mapping is a coin flip per seed and
  averages to chance however well the index separates. Scored as
  |p(slot0 | lesson A) - p(slot0 | lesson B)|: 0 is no information, 1 is
  perfect separation. `ctxfour` drew the same line -- a perfect index holds
  four DISTINCTIONS, not four MAPPINGS.
    derived-AB    too few creatures
    derived-keep  too few creatures
    derived2-AB   too few creatures
    derived2-keep too few creatures
    derived3-AB   too few creatures
    derived3-keep too few creatures
    A separation near 0 refutes THIS INDEX as a carrier. A separation well
    above 0 with chance AGREEMENT means the index works and only the
    slot->half assignment is arbitrary -- which is a fixable wiring problem,
    not a refutation.

  AGREEMENT GUARD -- did the mask land where the live lesson wanted?
    oracle  1.000   (must be 1.000 by construction)
    derived 0.000   <- THE WHOLE QUESTION
    latched 0.000   <- THE PREDICTION: reading the index while the
                     creature HEARS should raise this well above 0.720

